{"video_id":"Jj8DNLA5hYc","title":"Making Topology-Aware Scheduling Practical for AI Workloads: From Discovery to Simula... Weizhou Lan","conference":"kubecon","language":"en","auto_generated":true,"source":"supa","timing":"exact","word_count":2429,"segments":[{"start":0.32,"duration":5.08,"text":"Thank you for joining my session and"},{"start":3.28,"duration":5.36,"text":"today I would like to"},{"start":5.4,"duration":6.24,"text":"give a talk, give a session about"},{"start":8.64,"duration":6.64,"text":"making topology aware scheduling"},{"start":11.64,"duration":8.64,"text":"practical for AI workloads from"},{"start":15.28,"duration":8.64,"text":"discovery to simulation at scale."},{"start":20.28,"duration":7.28,"text":"Uh, I'm Weijie Lan and"},{"start":23.92,"duration":3.64,"text":"senior tech lead at"},{"start":28.64,"duration":5.16,"text":"discuss the goes beyond the the"},{"start":31.32,"duration":6.0,"text":"scheduler. It includes uh, network"},{"start":33.8,"duration":5.84,"text":"topology discovery and cost"},{"start":37.32,"duration":7.52,"text":"effective approach for function"},{"start":39.64,"duration":5.2,"text":"validations. So, let's get started."},{"start":45.44,"duration":5.56,"text":"As we know in model training scenarios,"},{"start":48.56,"duration":5.56,"text":"uh, networking communication volume is"},{"start":51.0,"duration":5.56,"text":"enormous uh, for conventional dense"},{"start":54.12,"duration":5.08,"text":"models such as Llama"},{"start":56.56,"duration":6.0,"text":"or reduce communication uh,"},{"start":59.2,"duration":5.8,"text":"uh, dominate in this pattern. Uh, data"},{"start":62.56,"duration":6.68,"text":"exchange uh, typically occurs among the"},{"start":65.0,"duration":7.08,"text":"GPUs within each single network area. As"},{"start":69.24,"duration":5.84,"text":"a result, most uh, traffic can be"},{"start":72.08,"duration":6.44,"text":"handled locally by leaf switches."},{"start":75.08,"duration":7.32,"text":"In contrast, MoE models like Deep Seek"},{"start":78.52,"duration":6.24,"text":"routes data to different uh, experts and"},{"start":82.4,"duration":4.2,"text":"generates intensive all-to-all"},{"start":84.76,"duration":5.2,"text":"communication."},{"start":86.6,"duration":6.76,"text":"This traffic frequently traverses the"},{"start":89.96,"duration":6.12,"text":"upper tier switches to reach destination"},{"start":93.36,"duration":5.8,"text":"across different areas. Uh,"},{"start":96.08,"duration":6.16,"text":"consequently, uh, in a large-scale"},{"start":99.16,"duration":6.0,"text":"cluster, uh, workloads must be placed in"},{"start":102.24,"duration":6.76,"text":"an orderly manner according to the"},{"start":105.16,"duration":6.32,"text":"topology to avoid network"},{"start":109.0,"duration":5.96,"text":"congestion."},{"start":111.48,"duration":5.52,"text":"In inference scenarios, uh, complex RDMA"},{"start":114.96,"duration":3.56,"text":"traffic uh, patterns are also"},{"start":117.0,"duration":5.52,"text":"unavoidable."},{"start":118.52,"duration":7.16,"text":"Uh typical example is PD disaggregation,"},{"start":122.52,"duration":3.76,"text":"a prefilled and the decoder workloads"},{"start":125.68,"duration":4.0,"text":"um"},{"start":126.28,"duration":6.04,"text":"needed to synchronize KV cache data."},{"start":129.68,"duration":5.44,"text":"Uh so, they must uh be placed uh on"},{"start":132.32,"duration":5.48,"text":"topologically close nodes."},{"start":135.12,"duration":5.92,"text":"Uh this shortens the switch uh"},{"start":137.8,"duration":6.96,"text":"forwarding path and it helps avoid uh"},{"start":141.04,"duration":7.6,"text":"traffic conflicts uh with other jobs."},{"start":144.76,"duration":6.44,"text":"In addition, MOE model uh inference also"},{"start":148.64,"duration":4.68,"text":"involves all-to-all communication, often"},{"start":151.2,"duration":5.48,"text":"requiring traffic to"},{"start":153.32,"duration":7.64,"text":"traverse multiple layers of network"},{"start":156.68,"duration":5.4,"text":"topology. So, related tasks should be"},{"start":160.96,"duration":3.64,"text":"placed"},{"start":162.08,"duration":5.6,"text":"uh close together uh within the same"},{"start":164.6,"duration":4.2,"text":"network domain, and unrelated workloads"},{"start":167.68,"duration":4.48,"text":"should be"},{"start":168.8,"duration":7.04,"text":"uh spread out to uh minimize path level"},{"start":172.16,"duration":3.68,"text":"traffic contention."},{"start":175.92,"duration":5.92,"text":"Network traffic is further challenged by"},{"start":179.64,"duration":5.16,"text":"multi-tenant workloads."},{"start":181.84,"duration":7.04,"text":"In a multi-tenant environment, uh"},{"start":184.8,"duration":7.08,"text":"nothing is static. Uh we are constantly"},{"start":188.88,"duration":5.52,"text":"driven by requirements like canary"},{"start":191.88,"duration":6.48,"text":"releases and SLA."},{"start":194.4,"duration":7.76,"text":"To maximize GPU utilization, we cannot"},{"start":198.36,"duration":5.0,"text":"afford to isolate resources for each"},{"start":202.16,"duration":4.76,"text":"tenant."},{"start":203.36,"duration":5.96,"text":"Instead, um the cluster is treated as a"},{"start":206.92,"duration":5.24,"text":"single fluid pool."},{"start":209.32,"duration":6.04,"text":"Uh workloads from different tenants uh"},{"start":212.16,"duration":5.48,"text":"must be free to dynamically uh scale"},{"start":215.36,"duration":5.56,"text":"across all nodes."},{"start":217.64,"duration":5.04,"text":"Uh therefore, the flexibility comes with"},{"start":220.92,"duration":4.08,"text":"a challenge."},{"start":222.68,"duration":3.64,"text":"If workloads scale without topology"},{"start":225.0,"duration":4.04,"text":"awareness,"},{"start":226.32,"duration":6.8,"text":"uh network contention becomes"},{"start":229.04,"duration":7.08,"text":"inevitable. Uh or it can lead to unfair"},{"start":233.12,"duration":5.48,"text":"allocation of network resources uh,"},{"start":236.12,"duration":5.16,"text":"within certain parts of the topology"},{"start":238.6,"duration":6.04,"text":"among tenants."},{"start":241.28,"duration":6.4,"text":"To adjust this uh, challenges we've"},{"start":244.64,"duration":5.4,"text":"discussed the in in the past the slides,"},{"start":247.68,"duration":5.56,"text":"we need the intelligence topologies"},{"start":250.04,"duration":5.84,"text":"scheduling. It's no longer enough to"},{"start":253.24,"duration":5.84,"text":"uh, just to find the free slots. We must"},{"start":255.88,"duration":7.08,"text":"find the right slots. We rely on three"},{"start":259.08,"duration":6.68,"text":"core strategies. I think first pass"},{"start":262.96,"duration":6.4,"text":"isolation. We ensure that uh, unrelated"},{"start":265.76,"duration":4.92,"text":"AI workloads do not uh, contend with"},{"start":269.36,"duration":4.56,"text":"each other."},{"start":270.68,"duration":5.44,"text":"If a job A and a job B are independent,"},{"start":273.92,"duration":5.12,"text":"their traffic should never collide on"},{"start":276.12,"duration":4.32,"text":"the same network path as much as"},{"start":279.04,"duration":3.56,"text":"possible."},{"start":280.44,"duration":5.56,"text":"Second affinity."},{"start":282.6,"duration":6.48,"text":"For affinity sensitive workloads"},{"start":286.0,"duration":6.24,"text":"uh, like the prefilled and the decode"},{"start":289.08,"duration":5.88,"text":"pods, uh, distance is the enemy."},{"start":292.24,"duration":5.24,"text":"We make sure communication paths"},{"start":294.96,"duration":5.84,"text":"are as short as possible."},{"start":297.48,"duration":6.96,"text":"Third, health health uh, awareness."},{"start":300.8,"duration":6.32,"text":"Uh, network can fail and links can"},{"start":304.44,"duration":6.24,"text":"degrade. Our system should constantly"},{"start":307.12,"duration":6.24,"text":"monitor network health and triggers"},{"start":310.68,"duration":4.48,"text":"uh, disaster recovery rescheduling when"},{"start":313.36,"duration":3.08,"text":"necessary."},{"start":315.16,"duration":3.28,"text":"Um,"},{"start":316.44,"duration":5.0,"text":"um,"},{"start":318.44,"duration":5.6,"text":"ultimately we should like to uh, achieve"},{"start":321.44,"duration":6.44,"text":"several objectives um,"},{"start":324.04,"duration":7.44,"text":"to guarantee job SLAs by minimizing"},{"start":327.88,"duration":6.8,"text":"communication latency and to minimize"},{"start":331.48,"duration":6.2,"text":"uh, ROI ensuring that our"},{"start":334.68,"duration":6.84,"text":"uh, expensive network infrastructure is"},{"start":337.68,"duration":6.96,"text":"fully utilized and to ensure network"},{"start":341.52,"duration":6.6,"text":"resource uh, fairness among the tenants"},{"start":344.64,"duration":3.48,"text":"and the applications."},{"start":348.32,"duration":6.0,"text":"Uh, but it's the only native Cuba"},{"start":351.12,"duration":6.4,"text":"scheduler. Uh in some scenario simple"},{"start":354.32,"duration":5.92,"text":"scenarios, someone might consider using"},{"start":357.52,"duration":6.2,"text":"node label combined with pulse node"},{"start":360.24,"duration":5.64,"text":"affinity to control scheduling. Uh I"},{"start":363.72,"duration":5.24,"text":"think unfortunately,"},{"start":365.88,"duration":5.84,"text":"um this approach is fundamentally"},{"start":368.96,"duration":5.48,"text":"uh is unsuitable for AI workloads. Uh"},{"start":371.72,"duration":6.32,"text":"first the reason, manual orchestration"},{"start":374.44,"duration":7.48,"text":"overhead. Uh node affinity requires uh"},{"start":378.04,"duration":6.44,"text":"us to manually map a physical topology"},{"start":381.92,"duration":5.0,"text":"uh to logical labels. This depends"},{"start":384.48,"duration":4.92,"text":"heavily on human planning."},{"start":386.92,"duration":5.56,"text":"As the cluster grows, static partitions"},{"start":389.4,"duration":6.48,"text":"can cause conflicts between applications"},{"start":392.48,"duration":5.04,"text":"and operational costs quickly"},{"start":395.88,"duration":5.08,"text":"um um"},{"start":397.52,"duration":4.72,"text":"escalates. So, second reason, topology"},{"start":400.96,"duration":4.84,"text":"drift."},{"start":402.24,"duration":6.24,"text":"Labels are static metadata. They have no"},{"start":405.8,"duration":4.08,"text":"awareness of dynamic physical"},{"start":408.48,"duration":4.44,"text":"infrastructure."},{"start":409.88,"duration":6.12,"text":"If a network cable is removed or a"},{"start":412.92,"duration":5.32,"text":"switch is under maintenance,"},{"start":416.0,"duration":5.24,"text":"but the label isn't updated in real"},{"start":418.24,"duration":4.76,"text":"time, uh the scheduler is operating on a"},{"start":421.24,"duration":5.04,"text":"updated map."},{"start":423.0,"duration":4.64,"text":"Third reason, lack of hierarchical"},{"start":426.28,"duration":3.72,"text":"global view."},{"start":427.64,"duration":5.8,"text":"Node affinity is essentially set-based"},{"start":430.0,"duration":7.28,"text":"matching. It only knows whether a pod"},{"start":433.44,"duration":7.0,"text":"belongs to or does not belong to a node."},{"start":437.28,"duration":6.76,"text":"This flat view cannot represent a global"},{"start":440.44,"duration":6.92,"text":"network topology or quantify complex"},{"start":444.04,"duration":4.6,"text":"architecture. As a result, users often"},{"start":447.36,"duration":4.24,"text":"cannot"},{"start":448.64,"duration":6.4,"text":"uh define node affinity rules that truly"},{"start":451.6,"duration":6.12,"text":"reflect the physical network."},{"start":455.04,"duration":4.64,"text":"Final reason, gang scheduling."},{"start":457.72,"duration":4.16,"text":"It is a uh"},{"start":459.68,"duration":4.52,"text":"all or nothing game. Without the"},{"start":461.88,"duration":6.36,"text":"scheduling the entire group"},{"start":464.2,"duration":5.12,"text":"simultaneously, we may end up with the"},{"start":468.24,"duration":3.16,"text":"with"},{"start":469.32,"duration":5.08,"text":"partial allocation."},{"start":471.4,"duration":5.84,"text":"Some resources are locked while others"},{"start":474.4,"duration":7.2,"text":"are missing. It leads to"},{"start":477.24,"duration":7.12,"text":"resource deadlocks across the cluster."},{"start":481.6,"duration":4.56,"text":"On this slide, we outline the core"},{"start":484.36,"duration":3.04,"text":"requirements for topology-aware"},{"start":486.16,"duration":5.12,"text":"scheduling."},{"start":487.4,"duration":6.52,"text":"First, hierarchical topology view. The"},{"start":491.28,"duration":5.96,"text":"physical network is modeled as"},{"start":493.92,"duration":6.48,"text":"hierarchical key tree covering both"},{"start":497.24,"duration":6.8,"text":"scale-up and the scale-out architecture"},{"start":500.4,"duration":7.32,"text":"from smallest to largest. The typical"},{"start":504.04,"duration":5.76,"text":"hierarchy is node and a super pod and a"},{"start":507.72,"duration":4.88,"text":"rack and a spine."},{"start":509.8,"duration":5.08,"text":"Second, hard and soft topology"},{"start":512.6,"duration":4.96,"text":"constraints. First,"},{"start":514.88,"duration":6.16,"text":"hard constraints are strict. All pods of"},{"start":517.56,"duration":6.32,"text":"a job must stay must stay within a"},{"start":521.04,"duration":3.72,"text":"specific domain. If there's"},{"start":523.88,"duration":3.56,"text":"no"},{"start":524.76,"duration":3.88,"text":"sufficient nodes, the scheduling stays"},{"start":527.44,"duration":3.68,"text":"pending."},{"start":528.64,"duration":5.52,"text":"Soft constraints are flexible. The"},{"start":531.12,"duration":5.8,"text":"scheduler tries to pack pods tightly in"},{"start":534.16,"duration":5.8,"text":"a domain like rack"},{"start":536.92,"duration":5.28,"text":"and only spills over to adjacent domains"},{"start":539.96,"duration":5.0,"text":"if necessary."},{"start":542.2,"duration":6.28,"text":"Third, optimize the switch path for"},{"start":544.96,"duration":6.84,"text":"communication. For workloads like"},{"start":548.48,"duration":7.12,"text":"ML inference or PD"},{"start":551.8,"duration":6.04,"text":"aggregated tasks, we should place pods"},{"start":555.6,"duration":3.4,"text":"close close together within the same"},{"start":557.84,"duration":3.2,"text":"domain."},{"start":559.0,"duration":5.28,"text":"In the open source community,"},{"start":561.04,"duration":4.92,"text":"Volcano, Kai scheduler, and the queue"},{"start":564.28,"duration":4.4,"text":"already support the topology-aware"},{"start":565.96,"duration":6.08,"text":"scheduling."},{"start":568.68,"duration":5.72,"text":"On this slide, we have queue and"},{"start":572.04,"duration":3.88,"text":"enhancement over the native Kube"},{"start":574.4,"duration":5.24,"text":"scheduler."},{"start":575.92,"duration":6.96,"text":"Queue acts as a a gatekeeper for job"},{"start":579.64,"duration":5.96,"text":"scheduling. We could use node labels to"},{"start":582.88,"duration":5.76,"text":"define a topologies that are deeply"},{"start":585.6,"duration":6.6,"text":"replicated lines to the a hierarchical"},{"start":588.64,"duration":6.72,"text":"network topology. Each cluster each"},{"start":592.2,"duration":6.28,"text":"cluster node is labeled accordingly. So"},{"start":595.36,"duration":7.0,"text":"Q can understand the logical topology."},{"start":598.48,"duration":8.92,"text":"We can specify hard hard"},{"start":602.36,"duration":9.0,"text":"or or soft topology constraints using"},{"start":607.4,"duration":7.32,"text":"annotation labels in the workload YAML."},{"start":611.36,"duration":6.36,"text":"When a job is submitted, Q first"},{"start":614.72,"duration":6.04,"text":"calculates the remaining capacity within"},{"start":617.72,"duration":6.12,"text":"the relevant topology domains. If"},{"start":620.76,"duration":7.56,"text":"sufficient resources are available, Q"},{"start":623.84,"duration":7.88,"text":"injects node selectors or pod affinity"},{"start":628.32,"duration":6.96,"text":"to pod templates. This guides the native"},{"start":631.72,"duration":6.8,"text":"kube scheduler to make placement with"},{"start":635.28,"duration":5.96,"text":"decisions that respect the topology"},{"start":638.52,"duration":2.72,"text":"constraints."},{"start":641.28,"duration":4.16,"text":"Now, we are"},{"start":642.76,"duration":6.36,"text":"uh let's look at the Volcano. Volcano"},{"start":645.44,"duration":6.92,"text":"serves as a replacement for the default"},{"start":649.12,"duration":7.4,"text":"kube scheduler. It builds a logical"},{"start":652.36,"duration":8.52,"text":"topology tree using hypernodes CRD. We"},{"start":656.52,"duration":9.2,"text":"can manually assign labels to nodes for"},{"start":660.88,"duration":8.0,"text":"each switch tier of the topology and uh"},{"start":665.72,"duration":6.84,"text":"Volcano will automatically sync these"},{"start":668.88,"duration":6.64,"text":"updates to the hypernode instances at"},{"start":672.56,"duration":6.8,"text":"periodical intervals."},{"start":675.52,"duration":6.96,"text":"When uh submitting a Volcano job, uh we"},{"start":679.36,"duration":7.12,"text":"use the network topology field to"},{"start":682.48,"duration":7.28,"text":"specify a topology constraints."},{"start":686.48,"duration":7.28,"text":"I think a key advantage of Volcano is"},{"start":689.76,"duration":6.12,"text":"the integration of InfiniBand InfiniBand"},{"start":693.76,"duration":5.6,"text":"topology discovery."},{"start":695.88,"duration":6.68,"text":"Uh Volcano can interface directly with"},{"start":699.36,"duration":6.2,"text":"the InfiniBand UFM"},{"start":702.56,"duration":6.84,"text":"to automatically pull the network"},{"start":705.56,"duration":4.8,"text":"topology. This eliminate This elim-"},{"start":709.4,"duration":4.24,"text":"elim- um"},{"start":710.36,"duration":6.68,"text":"eliminates the manual effort of"},{"start":713.64,"duration":3.4,"text":"maintaining node labels."},{"start":717.76,"duration":4.12,"text":"On this slide, we introduce CAR"},{"start":720.6,"duration":5.12,"text":"scheduler"},{"start":721.88,"duration":6.64,"text":"developed by NVIDIA. Uh it's a a"},{"start":725.72,"duration":6.24,"text":"replacement for the default Kube"},{"start":728.52,"duration":7.56,"text":"scheduler. CAR scheduler use a topology"},{"start":731.96,"duration":5.72,"text":"CRD to understand how a network is"},{"start":736.08,"duration":3.84,"text":"uh structured."},{"start":737.68,"duration":6.32,"text":"Applications can define topology"},{"start":739.92,"duration":6.88,"text":"constraints either in pod group CRD or"},{"start":744.0,"duration":6.76,"text":"directly through pod annotations."},{"start":746.8,"duration":6.64,"text":"These constraints can be specified as"},{"start":750.76,"duration":4.36,"text":"required replacement or preferred"},{"start":753.44,"duration":4.12,"text":"replacement."},{"start":755.12,"duration":3.76,"text":"A key feature of CAR scheduler is"},{"start":757.56,"duration":4.76,"text":"subgroups."},{"start":758.88,"duration":6.36,"text":"Within a pod group, subgroup allow"},{"start":762.32,"duration":5.36,"text":"multiple sets of pods to have their own"},{"start":765.24,"duration":4.24,"text":"the independent topology"},{"start":767.68,"duration":4.56,"text":"constraints"},{"start":769.48,"duration":5.84,"text":"while also enabling a group-wide"},{"start":772.24,"duration":5.04,"text":"constraints across all pods. This"},{"start":775.32,"duration":4.48,"text":"ensures that"},{"start":777.28,"duration":3.68,"text":"affinity-sensitive workloads are placed"},{"start":779.8,"duration":3.92,"text":"uh uh"},{"start":780.96,"duration":5.64,"text":"close together. Uh it is especially"},{"start":783.72,"duration":8.36,"text":"suitable for a pre-fuel and the decoder"},{"start":786.6,"duration":9.16,"text":"workloads in PD um disaggregation."},{"start":792.08,"duration":6.44,"text":"So, let's look uh let's look at the list"},{"start":795.76,"duration":6.0,"text":"uh typical topology example that"},{"start":798.52,"duration":4.52,"text":"combines with scale-up and scale-out"},{"start":801.76,"duration":4.28,"text":"networks."},{"start":803.04,"duration":4.68,"text":"As shown in the diagram, within each"},{"start":806.04,"duration":5.36,"text":"GB200,"},{"start":807.72,"duration":7.36,"text":"every 72 GPUs are interconnected"},{"start":811.4,"duration":7.48,"text":"via NV switch to form a super pod."},{"start":815.08,"duration":8.56,"text":"Nvidia refers to this as multi-node"},{"start":818.88,"duration":7.28,"text":"NVLink domain or NVL domain. These super"},{"start":823.64,"duration":5.4,"text":"pods are also interconnected"},{"start":826.16,"duration":6.0,"text":"through rack and a spine switch,"},{"start":829.04,"duration":6.96,"text":"forming a scale-out fabric."},{"start":832.16,"duration":8.0,"text":"So, the topology hierarchy"},{"start":836.0,"duration":5.28,"text":"from smallest to largest is node, super"},{"start":840.16,"duration":3.68,"text":"pod,"},{"start":841.28,"duration":6.32,"text":"rack, and spine."},{"start":843.84,"duration":7.0,"text":"Now, suppose we are deploying a group of"},{"start":847.6,"duration":6.44,"text":"vRAM inference instances. As shown in"},{"start":850.84,"duration":6.4,"text":"the YAML on the right of the slide, we"},{"start":854.04,"duration":6.96,"text":"can apply a hard topology constraints to"},{"start":857.24,"duration":6.32,"text":"ensure that the entire workload stays"},{"start":861.0,"duration":6.64,"text":"within a single rack domain"},{"start":863.56,"duration":8.24,"text":"regardless of how it scales. And we"},{"start":867.64,"duration":7.72,"text":"adopt a bin pack strategy and apply soft"},{"start":871.8,"duration":6.92,"text":"topology constraints to keep instances"},{"start":875.36,"duration":7.4,"text":"tightly grouped within a few adjacent"},{"start":878.72,"duration":5.76,"text":"super pods. This allows communication to"},{"start":882.76,"duration":5.4,"text":"fully leverage the performance"},{"start":884.48,"duration":5.24,"text":"advantages of of NV switch within the"},{"start":888.16,"duration":6.0,"text":"super pod."},{"start":889.72,"duration":7.76,"text":"As a result, all pods are deployed in a"},{"start":894.16,"duration":7.12,"text":"structured manner."},{"start":897.48,"duration":6.76,"text":"So far, we would discuss the advanced"},{"start":901.28,"duration":7.96,"text":"schedulers. They are powerful, but they"},{"start":904.24,"duration":8.6,"text":"are also one critical dependency is"},{"start":909.24,"duration":6.32,"text":"node label for each topology layer."},{"start":912.84,"duration":5.68,"text":"These node labels represent the logical"},{"start":915.56,"duration":5.92,"text":"mapping of underlying network topology"},{"start":918.52,"duration":5.76,"text":"hierarchy. If the labels are wrong, the"},{"start":921.48,"duration":4.28,"text":"scheduling decision will be wrong."},{"start":924.28,"duration":3.0,"text":"Humans cannot"},{"start":925.76,"duration":3.68,"text":"reliably"},{"start":927.28,"duration":5.4,"text":"integrate complex the network"},{"start":929.44,"duration":6.68,"text":"topologies. It is not a reliable to"},{"start":932.68,"duration":7.68,"text":"manually label node at scale. That's why"},{"start":936.12,"duration":7.12,"text":"we need a topology detector or builder."},{"start":940.36,"duration":5.08,"text":"Think of it as the bridge"},{"start":943.24,"duration":4.52,"text":"between your physical network"},{"start":945.44,"duration":6.2,"text":"infrastructure and the Kubernetes. It"},{"start":947.76,"duration":5.48,"text":"runs inside the cluster and solves two"},{"start":951.64,"duration":4.68,"text":"key problems."},{"start":953.24,"duration":6.72,"text":"First, network auto discovery. It"},{"start":956.32,"duration":6.12,"text":"connects directly to external systems"},{"start":959.96,"duration":6.52,"text":"such as InfiniBand"},{"start":962.44,"duration":5.36,"text":"fabric manager or NVLink manager tools"},{"start":966.48,"duration":4.68,"text":"and uh"},{"start":967.8,"duration":5.08,"text":"automatically discovers how the network"},{"start":971.16,"duration":4.72,"text":"is wired"},{"start":972.88,"duration":5.84,"text":"uh from scale-out switches down to"},{"start":975.88,"duration":6.32,"text":"scale-up GPU internet connects. It"},{"start":978.72,"duration":7.28,"text":"builds an accurate topology view and it"},{"start":982.2,"duration":5.16,"text":"tells us uh the position of each node"},{"start":986.0,"duration":5.4,"text":"within the"},{"start":987.36,"duration":5.24,"text":"uh different network hierarchy levels."},{"start":991.4,"duration":3.88,"text":"Second,"},{"start":992.6,"duration":6.92,"text":"uh network health awareness."},{"start":995.28,"duration":5.68,"text":"It is not enough to know a link exists."},{"start":999.52,"duration":3.24,"text":"We need to know"},{"start":1000.96,"duration":6.12,"text":"it works."},{"start":1002.76,"duration":6.12,"text":"If a cable is uh degraded or a switch"},{"start":1007.08,"duration":3.52,"text":"port fails,"},{"start":1008.88,"duration":5.24,"text":"the detector should"},{"start":1010.6,"duration":5.64,"text":"identify it immediately and update node"},{"start":1014.12,"duration":4.64,"text":"status accordingly"},{"start":1016.24,"duration":5.2,"text":"so the scheduler can make the right"},{"start":1018.76,"duration":2.68,"text":"decision."},{"start":1021.92,"duration":5.12,"text":"Now, let's look at the uh topology"},{"start":1024.56,"duration":4.28,"text":"detector solution from NVIDIA network"},{"start":1027.04,"duration":3.04,"text":"environments."},{"start":1028.84,"duration":2.6,"text":"NVIDIA"},{"start":1030.08,"duration":2.36,"text":"topograph"},{"start":1031.44,"duration":2.2,"text":"it"},{"start":1032.44,"duration":3.36,"text":"it"},{"start":1033.64,"duration":3.48,"text":"automates the entire workflow uh"},{"start":1035.8,"duration":3.84,"text":"workflow."},{"start":1037.12,"duration":3.68,"text":"It supports the full NVIDIA networking"},{"start":1039.64,"duration":5.12,"text":"stack."},{"start":1040.8,"duration":7.16,"text":"When you're running uh RoCE on Spectrum"},{"start":1044.76,"duration":4.56,"text":"switches or InfiniBand on Quantum"},{"start":1047.96,"duration":4.56,"text":"switches"},{"start":1049.32,"duration":6.52,"text":"or leveraging NVLink switch for scale-up"},{"start":1052.52,"duration":5.48,"text":"connectivity, it has visibility"},{"start":1055.84,"duration":2.76,"text":"across all fabrics."},{"start":1058.0,"duration":2.6,"text":"It"},{"start":1058.6,"duration":4.8,"text":"continuously talks to network"},{"start":1060.6,"duration":5.4,"text":"infrastructure. It builds an accurate"},{"start":1063.4,"duration":5.32,"text":"topology map and the light it"},{"start":1066.0,"duration":5.6,"text":"automatically applies multiple topology"},{"start":1068.72,"duration":4.64,"text":"labels to each node."},{"start":1071.6,"duration":4.8,"text":"Each label represents the node's"},{"start":1073.36,"duration":7.52,"text":"position at each level of the network"},{"start":1076.4,"duration":7.6,"text":"uh hierarchy like super pod, uh rack,"},{"start":1080.88,"duration":8.36,"text":"and the spine. Uh because this process"},{"start":1084.0,"duration":8.52,"text":"is automated and uh synchronized with uh"},{"start":1089.24,"duration":4.96,"text":"the with the fabric, the labels stay"},{"start":1092.52,"duration":4.48,"text":"accurate."},{"start":1094.2,"duration":6.16,"text":"So, scheduler like a cast scheduler can"},{"start":1097.0,"duration":6.88,"text":"immediately uh make right decision of"},{"start":1100.36,"duration":7.08,"text":"topology aware scheduling."},{"start":1103.88,"duration":7.4,"text":"So, what if your network hardware comes"},{"start":1107.44,"duration":6.96,"text":"comes with vendors other than NVIDIA?"},{"start":1111.28,"duration":5.6,"text":"In a non-NVIDIA network environments,"},{"start":1114.4,"duration":4.96,"text":"uh we may need to develop a custom a"},{"start":1116.88,"duration":5.88,"text":"custom topology builder."},{"start":1119.36,"duration":8.48,"text":"For the scale-out network, many problems"},{"start":1122.76,"duration":7.24,"text":"many modern switches uh run Sonic OS."},{"start":1127.84,"duration":6.4,"text":"Uh topology builder can query the"},{"start":1130.0,"duration":7.56,"text":"switches via GNMI protocol to collect"},{"start":1134.24,"duration":6.52,"text":"all the network neighbor information."},{"start":1137.56,"duration":7.96,"text":"For the scale-up fabric, each GPU vendor"},{"start":1140.76,"duration":7.24,"text":"repre- uh provides CLI tools or API to"},{"start":1145.52,"duration":4.56,"text":"expose domain IDs."},{"start":1148.0,"duration":4.12,"text":"By collecting these uh"},{"start":1150.08,"duration":5.0,"text":"IDs, we can"},{"start":1152.12,"duration":6.56,"text":"uh determine which GPU are physically"},{"start":1155.08,"duration":6.28,"text":"interconnected by scale-up network."},{"start":1158.68,"duration":6.64,"text":"Therefore, they can build an accurate"},{"start":1161.36,"duration":9.08,"text":"topology map and apply multiple topology"},{"start":1165.32,"duration":7.96,"text":"labels to each node for the scheduler."},{"start":1170.44,"duration":5.48,"text":"Now, we are facing"},{"start":1173.28,"duration":4.24,"text":"validation challenge across multiple"},{"start":1175.92,"duration":5.92,"text":"scenarios."},{"start":1177.52,"duration":7.64,"text":"First, scenario for scheduling decision."},{"start":1181.84,"duration":6.16,"text":"For instance, after deploying and"},{"start":1185.16,"duration":6.0,"text":"configuring the scheduler, we need"},{"start":1188.0,"duration":5.56,"text":"clearly we need a clear visibility into"},{"start":1191.16,"duration":3.44,"text":"its scheduling behavior."},{"start":1193.56,"duration":4.6,"text":"And"},{"start":1194.6,"duration":6.92,"text":"second, uh like scenarios for network"},{"start":1198.16,"duration":6.12,"text":"topology construction. For instance, if"},{"start":1201.52,"duration":6.28,"text":"we want to develop a custom topology"},{"start":1204.28,"duration":8.04,"text":"builder, we need an environment for"},{"start":1207.8,"duration":7.76,"text":"developing and testing. So, we need a a"},{"start":1212.32,"duration":7.6,"text":"network environment environment with"},{"start":1215.56,"duration":7.88,"text":"rich and realistic topology layers"},{"start":1219.92,"duration":5.12,"text":"covering both scale-up and scale-out"},{"start":1223.44,"duration":5.88,"text":"architectures."},{"start":1225.04,"duration":8.36,"text":"However, it may require a dozens of"},{"start":1229.32,"duration":6.52,"text":"switches or GPU servers. The cost is uh"},{"start":1233.4,"duration":4.16,"text":"prohibitive"},{"start":1235.84,"duration":5.4,"text":"prohibitive."},{"start":1237.56,"duration":7.6,"text":"So, when it comes to validating the"},{"start":1241.24,"duration":8.84,"text":"schedulers like Kai scheduler,"},{"start":1245.16,"duration":7.52,"text":"we can how we can access a GPU cluster"},{"start":1250.08,"duration":4.32,"text":"with a multi multi-layer network"},{"start":1252.68,"duration":5.68,"text":"topology."},{"start":1254.4,"duration":6.88,"text":"My answer is It is It mean means"},{"start":1258.36,"duration":4.56,"text":"Kubernetes without the Kubelet."},{"start":1261.28,"duration":4.64,"text":"Uh functionally,"},{"start":1262.92,"duration":5.72,"text":"simulates the behavior of the"},{"start":1265.92,"duration":5.52,"text":"Kubelet. It allows"},{"start":1268.64,"duration":5.96,"text":"developers to generate thousands of"},{"start":1271.44,"duration":4.72,"text":"virtual nodes inside a kind cluster"},{"start":1274.6,"duration":4.32,"text":"within seconds."},{"start":1276.16,"duration":4.6,"text":"These virtual nodes can be configured"},{"start":1278.92,"duration":5.08,"text":"with"},{"start":1280.76,"duration":6.4,"text":"arbitrary resource specifications such"},{"start":1284.0,"duration":6.32,"text":"as GPUs or memory"},{"start":1287.16,"duration":4.8,"text":"regardless of the actual actual host"},{"start":1290.32,"duration":5.36,"text":"hardware."},{"start":1291.96,"duration":6.72,"text":"When a pod is scheduled to a node"},{"start":1295.68,"duration":5.4,"text":"immediately updates the pod"},{"start":1298.68,"duration":3.6,"text":"status to running."},{"start":1301.08,"duration":4.96,"text":"But no"},{"start":1302.28,"duration":6.96,"text":"actual containers are started. The"},{"start":1306.04,"duration":5.4,"text":"mechanism operates entirely at the"},{"start":1309.24,"duration":5.44,"text":"control plane level."},{"start":1311.44,"duration":6.24,"text":"Uh with cap at least with this cap"},{"start":1314.68,"duration":6.76,"text":"capability, we can label the virtual"},{"start":1317.68,"duration":9.76,"text":"nodes with topology tire"},{"start":1321.44,"duration":8.0,"text":"attributes such as spine or rack. So, we"},{"start":1327.44,"duration":5.12,"text":"we learn deploy kind scheduler in the"},{"start":1329.44,"duration":5.72,"text":"kind cluster and submit simulated"},{"start":1332.56,"duration":6.08,"text":"inference workloads to these virtual"},{"start":1335.16,"duration":6.04,"text":"nodes. Well, at least allows us to"},{"start":1338.64,"duration":6.12,"text":"accurately verify validate the"},{"start":1341.2,"duration":6.52,"text":"scheduling results."},{"start":1344.76,"duration":6.44,"text":"When we are developing and testing a"},{"start":1347.72,"duration":6.4,"text":"custom topology builder for non-Nvidia"},{"start":1351.2,"duration":4.24,"text":"network environments, the the builder"},{"start":1354.12,"duration":4.96,"text":"needs to"},{"start":1355.44,"duration":7.24,"text":"actually communicate with switches at"},{"start":1359.08,"duration":5.52,"text":"different network layer and construct a"},{"start":1362.68,"duration":5.76,"text":"network topology."},{"start":1364.6,"duration":7.8,"text":"This means we must have real switch"},{"start":1368.44,"duration":6.0,"text":"available. So, how do we obtain such a"},{"start":1372.4,"duration":5.4,"text":"Kubernetes cluster?"},{"start":1374.44,"duration":5.92,"text":"My My practical solution is Nvidia Air."},{"start":1377.8,"duration":5.76,"text":"Nvidia Air is a free SaaS platform to"},{"start":1380.36,"duration":6.4,"text":"simulating network infrastructure of a"},{"start":1383.56,"duration":6.44,"text":"data center. It allows It allows us to"},{"start":1386.76,"duration":7.32,"text":"deploy Linux VM and the virtual Ethernet"},{"start":1390.0,"duration":6.6,"text":"switches with Sonic OS or"},{"start":1394.08,"duration":7.2,"text":"Cumulus OS. So, we can build a"},{"start":1396.6,"duration":8.92,"text":"multi-layer network topology exactly as"},{"start":1401.28,"duration":6.12,"text":"we desire and deploy Kubernetes directly"},{"start":1405.52,"duration":4.72,"text":"on top of it."},{"start":1407.4,"duration":5.6,"text":"We can deploy our custom topology"},{"start":1410.24,"duration":6.84,"text":"builder on a cluster. It can communicate"},{"start":1413.0,"duration":6.76,"text":"with the switch to collect"},{"start":1417.08,"duration":5.84,"text":"topology information and the generate a"},{"start":1419.76,"duration":7.36,"text":"hierarchical node labels."},{"start":1422.92,"duration":6.0,"text":"In addition, NVIDIA provides APIs to"},{"start":1427.12,"duration":4.32,"text":"automatically"},{"start":1428.92,"duration":6.28,"text":"create infrastructure based on"},{"start":1431.44,"duration":7.24,"text":"user-defined topology configurations."},{"start":1435.2,"duration":6.44,"text":"This makes it easy to"},{"start":1438.68,"duration":5.64,"text":"to build a CI pipelines for"},{"start":1441.64,"duration":4.44,"text":"automatically testing."},{"start":1444.32,"duration":4.44,"text":"Okay. Uh"},{"start":1446.08,"duration":5.16,"text":"Uh that's all of my presentation and"},{"start":1448.76,"duration":2.48,"text":"thank you."},{"start":1452.2,"duration":2.6,"text":"Any questions?"}]}